    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter today with a clear hierarchy of efficiency, led by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.11). **Gunnar Henderson** remains our primary offensive engine; despite a slight drag from the catcher\u2019s arm efficiency, he benefits immensely from a favorable park factor and a solid matchup against Painter. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** finds himself in an ideal spot against Elder, leveraging a dynamic platoon advantage and a premium spot in the order to solidify his status as a \"Strong\" play. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** also anchors the daily output (68.80), as his plate discipline and power profile project well against Leahy despite the modest park adjustment.\n\nOur rotation decisions today heavily favor high-volume order positions, with **Sam Antonacci** (61.43) and **Liam Hicks** (59.93) securing spots due to their leadoff status against questionable starters like Martinez and Senga. **Jacob Wilson** (65.19) is a high-value play if confirmed in the #2 hole, as his projection thrives on current momentum. The most difficult personnel decision was benching **Luis Robert Jr.** (52.06); while his raw power is undeniable, a significant negative platoon adjustment against Junk pushed him just below the threshold required to displace our current outfield configuration. His profile remains in flux pending further data on his platoon splits.\n\nWe are monitoring several \"Lineup Pending\" statuses, specifically for **Jacob Wilson**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Andy Pages**, and **Luis Lara**. **Kyle Tucker** (54.57) and **Andy Pages** (53.71) face a difficult test against Ranger Suarez, where the elite opposing skill is actively depressing their projections. We are banking on the fact that their daily floors are high enough to justify the start, though the risk of an early-game deficit or limited high-leverage opportunities persists. Investors should watch the final lineups closely, as any shift in batting order for these players could drastically alter their path to the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold.",
